\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Anatomy of an EACS admit card. The upper band carries institutional branding and the examination title; the central block contains the nine transcribed fields; the lower band lists registered subjects and their numeric codes. Field geometry is fixed by the card template, so the regions shown here are stable across the whole corpus.}}{4}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
